  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical Assistance for Carbon Border Adjustment Mechanism good exports from UA to EU</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall purpose of the project is to strengthen the export capacity of Ukrainian (UA) producers coming from economic sectors that currently export or plan to export goods to the European Union (EU) under the Carbon Border Adjustment Mechanism (CBAM): iron and steel, cement, fertilizers and aluminium. A pilot will be set up with three selected producers coming from these sectors to correctly determine the direct and indirect embedded emissions of the produced CBAM goods in the framework of the EU methodology. The pilot project will help Ukrainian producers to build capacity for export to the EU under CBAM regulations and to reduce GHG emissions of their installations as well as empower actions for greenhouse gas (GHG) emissions mitigation.Through technical assistance, these three producers will be used as a case for drafting tailormade guidelines documents on CBAM that will be available for other Ukrainian producers and businesses of the selected economic sectors. The results of this project will be further disseminated via online events, one for each of the export sectors that were selected for piloting.  The project has a positive impact on:SDG 8: inclusive and sustainable economic growth: support productive activities, decent job creation, entrepreneurship, creativity and innovation.SDG 13: Climate action: national climate policies, and resources to create awareness and support for climate change mitigation measures to reduce GHG emissions.</narrative>
  </description>
